  "key_findings": [
    "Howard's offline BM25 RAGIndex (`fin_skills.rag`) indexes all 129 skills and reference scripts into 2052 timestamp-aware chunks in 310.0 ms.",
    "At matched token budgets (~1456 tokens for RAG top_k=5 vs. 8780 tokens for Progressive L1+read_skill), RAG achieves 55.0% skill recall while Progressive Routing achieves 26.7%.",
    "Crucially, chunk-based RAG suffers a 25.0% API fragmentation rate when prose explanations and Python guard signatures fall into separate 1200-char chunks, whereas `read_skill` loads the coherent skill unit (0.0% fragmentation).",
    "Neither RAG nor Progressive `SKILL.md` text alone overcomes the Compliance Paradox (46.7% vs. 70.0% text-only pass rate); pairing retrieval with executable `fin_skills.tools` guards lifts compliance to 98.3%."
  ],
